# Environment Variables Template

## Backend (.env)

```env
# =======================
# SERVER CONFIGURATION
# =======================
PORT=5000
NODE_ENV=development

# =======================
# DATABASE CONFIGURATION
# =======================
MONGODB_URI=mongodb://localhost:27017/chess-game
# Alternative for MongoDB Atlas:
# MONGODB_URI=mongodb+srv://username:password@cluster0.xxxxx.mongodb.net/chess-game

# =======================
# AUTHENTICATION
# =======================
JWT_SECRET=your_super_secret_jwt_key_change_this_in_production_to_a_random_string
JWT_EXPIRE=7d

# =======================
# CORS CONFIGURATION
# =======================
FRONTEND_URL=http://localhost:3000

# =======================
# WEBSOCKET CONFIGURATION
# =======================
WS_PORT=5000

# =======================
# OPTIONAL: API KEYS
# =======================
# Add any third-party API keys here if needed
```

## Frontend (.env.local)

```env
# =======================
# API CONFIGURATION
# =======================
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:5000
NEXT_PUBLIC_WS_URL=ws://localhost:5000

# =======================
# DEBUG MODE (optional)
# =======================
NEXT_PUBLIC_DEBUG=false
```

---

## Production Guidelines

### Backend Production .env
```env
PORT=5000
NODE_ENV=production

# Use MongoDB Atlas
MONGODB_URI=mongodb+srv://username:password@cluster.mongodb.net/chess-game?retryWrites=true&w=majority

# Generate a strong secret key
JWT_SECRET=your_production_secret_key_minimum_32_characters_recommended

# Use HTTPS frontend URL
FRONTEND_URL=https://yourdomain.com

# Enable HTTPS for WebSocket
WS_PORT=443
WS_URL=wss://yourdomain.com
```

### Frontend Production .env.production.local
```env
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://api.yourdomain.com
NEXT_PUBLIC_WS_URL=wss://api.yourdomain.com
```

---

## Security Notes

1. **JWT_SECRET**: Generate with: `node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"`
2. **Never commit .env files**: Use .env.example and .gitignore
3. **Database Credentials**: Use environment variables, not hardcoded
4. **HTTPS in Production**: Always use SSL/TLS
5. **CORS**: Restrict to specific domains in production
6. **Rate Limiting**: Implement on API endpoints

---

## Development vs Production

| Setting | Development | Production |
|---------|-------------|-----------|
| NODE_ENV | development | production |
| HTTPS | No | Yes |
| Debug Logs | Verbose | Minimal |
| CORS Origins | * (allow all) | Specific domains |
| Database | Local MongoDB | MongoDB Atlas |
| Error Messages | Detailed | Generic |
| Code Optimization | None | Minified/Compressed |
